:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/EVALUATION.md#when-a-finding-blocks-promotion"],"statement":"a valid falsification of a mandatory claim governed by a non-waivable hard stop — the boundary blocks, whatever the assigned priority or the decision cutoff","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:block-hard-stop-row"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:promotion-block","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must-not","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"literal":"by itself","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:condition"},{"literal":"the observation is repricing or re-entry input, returned as §4 states","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:forbids","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/EVALUATION.md#when-a-finding-blocks-promotion"],"statement":"an observation outside the exact reviewed claim — repricing or re-entry input, returned as §4 states: by itself it does not widen the reviewed subject, block its bounded claim, or require a new ticket, artifact, review round or implementation increment","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:block-outside-claim"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:policy-choice","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:promotion-block","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"literal":"EVALUATION §5; the cutoff: the adopting Product","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:owner"},{"literal":"below the Product-owned cutoff no block follows mechanically","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:choice"},{"literal":"mechanical blocking by severity, or the decision owner's act under a cutoff","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:among"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/EVALUATION.md#when-a-finding-blocks-promotion"],"statement":"any other finding meeting one of the four conditions — the decision owner decides blocking from the exact affected claim, the governed outcome or decision the work serves (ACTIVATION §1, Intake), the applicable hard stops and the Product-owned cutoff policy; below that cutoff no block follows mechanically, and an accepted residual is retained explicitly","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:block-owner-decides"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P2 Purpose. A selected outcome defines adequacy; interfaces inherit material obligations from the transformation they serve.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p2"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P6 Justification and authority. Definitions, assumptions, observations, candidate judgments and accepted claims have distinct standing; evidence supports a claim on a basis; authority permi